  "data": [
    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1954190696816288121",
      "url": "https://x.com/Resonant_News/status/1954190696816288121",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/Resonant_News/status/1954190696816288121",
      "text": "🚨 𝗕𝗥𝗘𝗔𝗞𝗜𝗡𝗚: 𝗕𝗲𝗶𝗷𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗔𝗰𝗰𝘂𝘀𝗲𝘀 𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗶𝗹𝗮 𝗼𝗳 '𝗣𝗹𝗮𝘆𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝘄𝗶𝘁𝗵 𝗙𝗶𝗿𝗲' 𝗔𝗺𝗶𝗱 𝗘𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗹𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗧𝗲𝗻𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀\n\n🇨🇳🇵🇭| China has sharply criticized the Philippines for \"playing with fire\" after President Ferdinand Marcos Jr stated during an India visit that Manila would likely get involved in any Taiwan conflict due to its geographic proximity and large Filipino diaspora there.\n\n💥 The Chinese foreign ministry protested, claiming such remarks violate the one-China principle, undermine regional stability, and breach international laws, urging the Philippines to avoid interfering in China's internal affairs.\n\n🔥 Marcos emphasized the need to protect Philippine territory and evacuate citizens from Taiwan in a crisis, while Manila reaffirmed its adherence to the one-China policy and non-interference stance.\n\n‼️ This exchange heightens ongoing frictions, including South China Sea disputes, as Beijing views the comments as damaging bilateral ties and regional peace.\n\n#ChinaPhilippines #TaiwanTensions #SouthChinaSea #OneChinaPolicy #IndoPacific",
